, "overview": "Michigan's open governor's race pits Democrat Jocelyn Benson against Republican John James, with term limits keeping Gretchen Whitmer off the ballot. Polls throughout October consistently show Benson ahead, with most surveys in the 5-to-13-point range and the strongest recent pollsters near +11. Benson has also raised about twice as much money as James and holds a wide cash advantage heading into the final stretch.\n\nRatings from across the spectrum cluster at Lean D or better, and prediction markets put Benson's win chances in the mid-90s. National Republicans reportedly pulled reserved ad time from the state, a sign of limited outside confidence in James. The main uncertainty is whether economic frustration over costs can tighten the race in the final days, but the evidence points to a Benson win with a margin near the high single digits.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9339, "margin": 7.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9166, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9224, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9193, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9053, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.911, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9221, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9131, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.912, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8925, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9071, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9049, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8998, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.8948, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.8922, "margin": 6.5}